  "details": "This is mostly a QoL change: Rather than providing the \"ID\" (order in the list) of a layer, it would be convenient to provide its name instead. Obviously there could be conflicts if two layers share the same name, but at that point it's on the user. \n\nMy suggestion is to provide the name field, and automatically convert it to the corresponding ID (First-found) once all third-party apps etc have done their things to the animator, and store it.",
